{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1344706-exile-angel","id":1344706,"title":"Exile Angel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-30T11:46:44-07:00","id":1344706,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Exile Angel","content":"I am creating a long-term antagonist and decided on an Exile Angel.<br /> <br /> The DtD core book has some great stuff. The Demon Storyteller's Guide (DSG) has more. I've tried to compile a list of &quot;attributes&quot; that an Exile could have. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> Eidetic Memory<br /> Perceive Infrastructure (Unseen sense merit?)<br /> Infrastructure presence: Gain +2 dice to activate Numina or reduce Essence by 1 and increase power over those with the Faith Condition (-2 to resist) DSG.81<br /> Can use Infrastructure to rain Essence like other Angels DSG.65<br /> Speak the first tongue like demons? DtD.183<br /> Don\u2019t worry about compromise (obviously!) DSG.65<br /> Can\u2019t create covers on their own (does this mean that a demon could create one for them?) DSG.65<br /> Perfect encyclopedic knowledge of every language ever devised (made up languages between twins for example?) DtD.183<br /> Immortal and not subject to disease DtD.32<br /> Might be able to hear and speak to the God-Machine DtD.51<br /> Sharper senses:<ul><li>Can see a broader range of electromagnetic radiation</li> <li>Hear the sound of a human\u2019s cells humming away beneath her skin</li> <li>Taste and smell the tiniest speck of organic matter</li> <li>Feel sharply enough to read print with their fingers or diagnose engine trouble by the vibrations traveling up the steering column</li> </ul>Faith condition grants a -2 mod to resist angelic powers or activities, including mundane effects such as Social maneuvering. DSG.81<br /> Can take on the shape of mortals. The corpse vanishes and the angel takes on the shape of a dead mortal. Must be before any mortal sees the body. DtD.73<br /> <br /> I did not include being a perfect liar as most Angels don't think about that way and don't have the opportunity or need to practice deception at the same level as demons.<br /> <br /> Let me know what the hive-mind thinks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T19:30:15-07:00","id":1344805,"title":"","content":"Exiles aren't plugged in, so they do not receive the various Numina benefits. Same issues with Hear and Speak to the God-Machine-not that angels hear and speak with the God-Machine anyways, even angels need Messengers to some degree.<br /> <br /> The Sharper senses might need Numen to account for it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise? Seems about right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T21:50:29-07:00","id":1344833,"title":"","content":"Angels don't have the ability to speak in all languages, (Demon Players Guide, p.28) , though they might have a numen that gives them the ability to speak in tongues, communicating in a universal fashion that transcends normal human languages.<br /> <br /> For me, designing an Exile would involve figuring out why/how they became an Exile, and how they maintain their Essence. The answer to those two question will do a lot in defining your Exile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T08:05:02-07:00","id":1344944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1344706-exile-angel?p=1344805#post1344805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exiles aren't plugged in, so they do not receive the various Numina benefits. Same issues with Hear and Speak to the God-Machine-not that angels hear and speak with the God-Machine anyways, even angels need Messengers to some degree.<br /> <br /> The Sharper senses might need Numen to account for it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise? Seems about right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the feedback!<br /> <br /> Regarding a custom Numen for the &quot;Sharper Senses&quot;. Zero cost (similar to Twilight Form) therefore being on all the time or would you think it would cost some Essence?<br /> <br /> Regarding the Numina benefits in the presence of Infrastructure, it makes sense that at least some of the &quot;access codes&quot; would be changed. But even the GM isn't full proof, yes?<br /> <br /> <b>--From DGS.80 </b><br /> Angels can install and use variations of Numina used by spirits and ghosts, but the reverse is not true. Non-angels lack the access codes for them to function.<br /> <br /> <br /> I did find this in DtD core book for Demon regarding the ability of Exiles to still hear and speak (possibly) to the GM.<br /> <br /> <b>--From DtD.51:</b><br /> Some exiles can still both hear and respond to the voice of the God-Machine. Others find they can hear their creator but cannot speak to it, or at the very least it does not choose to respond in turn.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't this indicate that there is still SOME connection?<br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps it's not an active connection but more of a &quot;I am this type, so ignore me&quot; kind of access. From my reading, it's kind of the Star Trek Borg interaction. GM-Connected Angels ignore/hinder you if you aren't a direct threat around infrastructure so you can go in, plug in (wirelessly?) and reap the benefits as long as you don't antagonize or get in their way.<br /> <br /> <b>--From DSG.64</b><br /> Angels try to distance themselves from the Abandoned and seem to know by instinct when they encounter an exile (though exiles themselves don\u2019t have that ability). Exiles have no support structures or organizations; whatever assistance they gained from Infrastructure or angels before their Abandonment is now barred. Loyal angels deter exiles from accessing secure locations, nonviolently when possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also reading DSG, it infers that an Angel may not know right away that they are an Exile.<br /> <br /> <b>--From DSG.64</b><br /> Once an angel realizes she has been Abandoned, the real struggle begins.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the languages, it seems like there is a possible contradiction, depending on how you read DtD.183. I would say that an Angel gets what she/he gets and simply &quot;abandoned&quot; would still have the language knowledge. Reading DSG.23 it says that they don't have the &quot;facility&quot;. I take that to mean that they don't need someone to grow up speaking a language for an Angel to know it (like a Demon does). They simply know all languages and can make themselves understood regardless.<br /> <br /> I back this up with DSG.28 further stating that the prevailing theory is that language itself is the output of a vast system of Infrastructure that exists beneath perceivable reality. ...one of the pillars of the God-Machine\u2019s power<br /> <br /> This would explain the severing of the ties between the Angel and GM: As manifestations of the God-Machine\u2019s will, angels interface with this system directly, distilling desire into pure meaning. Therefore, I think that an Exile could not &quot;communicate with everyone speaking different native languages in simultaneously but instead would need to translate to EACH language individually.<br /> <br /> <b>From DtD.183</b><br /> As agents of the God-Machine, every single angel is equipped with all talents and abilities necessary to perform their duty, <i>including a perfect encyclopedic knowledge of every language ever devised</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","user":"Ghostdriver","date":". 10-31-2019, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T13:17:05-07:00","id":1406499,"title":"","content":"Late to the party but I remember that angelic and demonic natural capacity for language is limited to those that have native speakers. It is even called out that demons have to go out of their way to learn dead languages or con-lang and do so because the machine's agents do not have an ingerent understanding of those languages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T10:32:24-07:00","id":1407154,"title":"","content":"I recall the DSG saying that angels can always make their instructions known to listeners, but they can't converse in every language. It's as if they speak in a &quot;divine language&quot; that humans can understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T15:27:30-07:00","id":1407195,"title":"","content":"Also, on the note of exiles not being able to make their own cover, I can't help but imagine what would happen if an exile performed an angel-jacking","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}